Colour a link from what its notebook actually did

Four faults, all of them the interface saying something it had not checked.

The lineage graph coloured its edges from the link's stored status, which
is written once at creation and never revisited, so every edge stayed
Planned no matter what the notebook did. It now takes the state computed
from real run history, and that history is read on load and refreshed
every twenty seconds while a run is in progress, so an edge changes
colour while the notebook is running rather than only after someone
opens Monitoring.

Recent runs showed three rows of Unknown. Run-on-demand returns 202
Accepted with no body, and each click pushed that empty object into the
history. It now reads the run list back from Fabric after the run is
accepted, which is also the only way to learn the instance id the empty
body never carried.

The grey rectangle under a notebook name was a status badge with class
names that do not exist - statusActive rather than stateActive - so the
badge kept its neutral background and its text was invisible against it.
It now goes through the same helper as every other status badge, which
is why the rest of the surface never had this.

The Ready badge in Monitoring hung off the panel edge because the stats
grid above it is inset by 16px and the message was not.

